Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence (AI) solution to enhance the efficiency of administrative services for the City of Belval. Our tailored approach leverages Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities, and a sovereign hosting infrastructure to provide intelligent assistance tools that are compliant with EU regulations, particularly GDPR, and contribute to environmental sustainability.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an AI-powered solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions, focusing on information consultation, drafting, file instruction, and collaboration. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure high availability (99.9%), response times under 2 seconds, and comply with GDPR and sovereignty requirements.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution integrates the contributions of all consortium members to deliver a coherent and comprehensive AI-powered assistance tool for the City of Belval's municipal agents.

- **Technical Architecture**: We will design a cloud-native architecture utilizing OVHcloud or Scaleway for sovereign hosting, ensuring compliance with SecNumCloud requirements. The frontend will be built using web frameworks (e.g., React), with an API gateway (Kong or Apigee) managing APIs and authentication. Microservices will be containerized using Docker and orchestrated with Kubernetes, allowing for scalability and high availability.
- **AI Components**: Our AIInnovation Agent proposes leveraging the Mistral 7B Instruct model, fine-tuned using LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning on a domain-specific corpus to adapt to the administrative context. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities will enable search and drafting assistance. We will employ dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse search, and hybrid approaches for information retrieval.
- **Security and Compliance**: To ensure GDPR compliance, we will host all data within the EU, enforce our cross-border transfer policy to prevent unauthorized data transfers, and utilize anonymization tools (Microsoft Presidio) and encryption (AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.3 in transit). Our access control standards include multi-factor authentication (TOTP or FIDO2), role-based access control, and privileged access management (CyberArk Conjur or HashiCorp Vault).
- **Integration**: We will integrate our solution with existing business software for civil status and town planning, electronic management of documents (EDM), and user directories using API standards like REST, GraphQL, SOAP, and CMIS.
- **Environmental Sustainability**: Our CSRSustainability Agent recommends utilizing green hosting partners (OVHcloud or Scaleway) that run on 100% renewable energy. Digital sobriety practices will include INT8/INT4 model quantization, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, estimated to reduce energy consumption by approximately 35%.
- **Budget and Cost**: Our Budget Agent confirms that our maximum contract value eligibility is €3,000,000, matching the project's global budget. Although specific costs for this project are not detailed, we will apply our pricing model to ensure a balanced approach between cost optimization and quality of service.
- **Deployment and Training**: The ProjectCoordinator Agent outlines a progressive deployment plan, starting with a pilot phase on a limited scope, followed by a generalization to all services. This will include accompaniment to change and training actions for agents to effectively use the new solution.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
